---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import GradientDivider from "../../components/GradientDivider.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Lunelia Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for the Lunelia housekeeping and home management app."
>
  <main class="home-page">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title">Lunelia Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="hero-text">Last updated: June 2026</p>
    </section>

    <GradientDivider />

    <section class="policy-grid">
      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>
          Lunelia is a housekeeping and home management application designed for
          iPhone, iPad, and other Apple devices. This privacy policy explains
          what information Lunelia stores, how it is used, and how your data
          remains under your control.
        </p>

        <p>
          Lunelia does not sell personal information, serve advertisements, or
          share your information with third parties for marketing purposes.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Data You Create</h2>
        <p>
          Information created within Lunelia may include chores, cleaning tasks,
          routines, room information, maintenance schedules, inventories,
          shopping lists, notes, rewards, achievements, points, and app
          preferences.
        </p>

        <p>
          This information is stored locally on your device and may synchronize
          through your personal iCloud account if CloudKit synchronization is
          enabled.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>iCloud & CloudKit</h2>
        <p>
          Lunelia may use Apple's CloudKit framework to synchronize information
          between your Apple devices through your personal iCloud account.
        </p>

        <p>
          The developer of Lunelia does not have access to your private CloudKit
          database.
        </p>

        <p>
          Apple's handling of iCloud data is governed by Apple's privacy policy.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Notifications</h2>
        <p>
          Lunelia uses local notifications to deliver reminders for chores,
          recurring cleaning schedules, maintenance activities, room resets, and
          other household responsibilities.
        </p>

        <p>
          Notification scheduling occurs directly on your device and
          notification content is not transmitted to external servers.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Widgets</h2>
        <p>
          Lunelia may provide Home Screen and Lock Screen widgets displaying
          cleaning progress, schedules, streaks, room information, points, and
          household insights.
        </p>

        <p>
          Widget information is shared locally between the app and widget
          extensions using Apple's App Group system.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Points, Rewards & Progress</h2>
        <p>
          Lunelia includes optional points, rewards, streaks, achievements, and
          progress systems designed to encourage consistency and motivation.
        </p>

        <p>
          This information remains private to your account and is not used for
          advertising or profiling purposes.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Shopping Lists & Inventories</h2>
        <p>
          If you choose to use shopping lists, inventory management, supply
          tracking, or restocking systems, this information is stored solely for
          your personal use and household organization.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Analytics & Tracking</h2>
        <p>
          Lunelia does not use advertising SDKs, third-party behavioral tracking
          systems, or targeted advertising technologies.
        </p>

        <p>
          Lunelia does not sell personal information and does not share your
          household data with advertisers.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>In-App Purchases</h2>
        <p>
          Lunelia may offer optional premium features or subscriptions through
          Apple's StoreKit framework.
        </p>

        <p>
          Payment processing is handled entirely by Apple. Lunelia does not
          collect, store, or have access to payment information, billing
          information, or credit card numbers.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Lunelia is not directed toward children under the age of 13 and does
          not knowingly collect personal information from children.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Data Deletion</h2>
        <p>
          You maintain control over your information at all times. Tasks,
          routines, schedules, inventories, notes, and other content may be
          deleted directly within the app.
        </p>

        <p>
          Deleting the app removes locally stored data from your device. If
          CloudKit synchronization is enabled, synced information may also be
          managed through your Apple ID and iCloud settings.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          This privacy policy may occasionally be updated to reflect new
          features, legal requirements, platform changes, or improvements to the
          app. Updated versions will be published on this page with a revised
          effective date.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions about this privacy policy or how Lunelia handles
          your information, you can contact:
        </p>

        <p>
          <a href="/contact" class="contact-button">Contact</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .policy-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding-bottom: 5rem;
  }

  .policy-card {
    background: var(--surface-standard);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 24px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .policy-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .policy-card h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--heading-small);
  }

  .policy-card p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .policy-card a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .contact-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
    color: var(--color-bg);
    border: 1px solid rgba(242, 239, 231, 0.12);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .contact-button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .policy-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .policy-card {
      padding: 1.25rem;
      border-radius: 20px;
    }
  }
</style>
